}
class Derived : Base {
}
```

If you call `new Derived().Create()`, it still creates a `Base` object, not a `Derived` object. Because `static` resolves to `Base` at compile time.

So the statement is correct: "Inside the parent class, the expression new static() always creates an object of the parent class."

